From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/25] IbashoAgent findAvatars and profile

An agent could only reach people it had already met: IMs, payments and
friendship offers take an avatar id, and nothing over LEAP turned a name
into one or read a profile.

findAvatars {name, limit=20, timeout=10} -> {avatars: [{id, username,
display_name}]} searches as the avatar picker does: the region's
AvatarPickerSearch capability, else the AvatarPickerRequest message with
a query id of our own, whose replies a hook in
LLFloaterAvatarPicker::processAvatarPickerReply hands over.

profile {id, timeout=10} reads a profile as the profile window does: the
AgentProfile capability, else the older AvatarPropertiesRequest (through
LLAvatarPropertiesProcessor) with picks asked for separately; the groups
and picks replies, which the processor ignores, reach it through two
hooks. Without the capability, groups or picks that don't come make the
reply partial.

Neither op opens a window, writes a file or messages anyone. Each
request's state is shared by its deferred reply and whatever fills it
in; the message routes stop listening when their request replies or
times out, and the properties observer is never destroyed, so the
processor's pointer to it can't dangle.
